<p>Thoughts: Would it be out-of-tone for, rather than a simple [REDACTED], for SCP-XXXX-1's mature phase to be a reflection of the host's &quot;true self&quot;, for lack of a better term, but distorted? An aggressive, violent person's SCP-XXXX-1 would be a hulking muscle-maniac, a greedy or predatory person's reflection turns lean and angular with a maw full of jagged teeth? Something that is still vaguely recognizable as you, but with your worst flaws exaggerated to a grotesque degree, could be even more disturbing than a completely inhuman monster.</p>

